I'll first verify how this component is consumed so the redesign stays compatible with its surroundings.Analysis complete. The component is rendered **only in compact mode** inside `timeline-card` (`ChatEntryTimeline.vue` → `ChatEntryTools :compact="true"`), so the summary row is the actual "wall" element users scan.

## Change Summary

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `file/path/to/ChatEntryTools.vue` | Replace the one-liner summary with a bordered "wall" block: status accent bar, mono tool name, status/duration/arg-count meta, plus an always-visible `key → value` params grid (3 visible, toggle for the rest) and an inline error line. Details block untouched. |

Design specs applied:
- **Layout:** left `border-l-2` status accent (info/success/error/neutral), `bg-base-200/40`, `rounded-r-md`, 8px-ish padding (`px-2.5 py-2`).
- **Hierarchy:** tool name `text-xs font-mono font-semibold` → params `text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wide /40` keys + `font-mono text-[11px] /70` values → duration `tabular-nums /50`.
- **Density:** grid `minmax(4.5rem,8rem) 1fr` keeps keys and values aligned column-wise so many events read as a continuous wall.
- **States:** hover tint, `aria-expanded` on both toggles, full value in `title` tooltip, no color-only meaning (icon + badge + accent bar).

