I need to locate the actual component that renders tool details under the chat entry menu, since the previous change was applied to a placeholder path.Now let me confirm how the tool details are surfaced from the chat entry menu.Found it — the tool details opened from the chat entry header (wrench `xN` button / "Events & Tools" menu item) are rendered by `src/components/chat/ChatMessageEvents.vue`, not by `ChatEntryTools.vue` (that one is only used by the legacy timeline).

## Change Summary

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `src/components/chat/ChatMessageEvents.vue` | Collapsed tool rows become a dense "wall": status accent bar per row, index, mono tool name, status, duration, timestamp and arg count on one line, plus an always-visible `key → value` params grid (3 rows + "+N more") and an inline error line. The expanded detail (Arguments / Result / Error / Output) is untouched. |

Design decisions:
- **Wall rhythm:** `divide-y` rows with `border-l-2` status accent (`info`/`success`/`error`/neutral) + `hover:bg-base-200/60` — the list reads as a continuous feed, not as separate cards.
- **Scannable columns:** params grid `minmax(4.5rem,7rem) 1fr` aligns keys/values down the wall; values are whitespace-collapsed, truncated at 72 chars with the full value in `title`.
- **No hidden meaning:** accent bar always paired with icon + status badge; the error text itself is printed in the summary (`line-clamp-2`).
- **Density:** `text-[10px]–text-xs`, `tabular-nums` for numbers, timestamp only from `@lg/panel` up.
- **Precomputed rows** in a `tools` computed (index, args, visible args, hidden count, time) so the per-row work isn't repeated 4× in the template.

